  "entry": "code/DF-XRM_vis_streamlit.py",
  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). Pick a crystal, an X-ray energy and a sample size; check how much beam gets through the sample; choose an (hkl) reflection; then see the 3D sample–beam–lens–goniometer geometry, read off the goniometer angles and lens-box position, and export them as a record to share with the beamline team and keep in the experiment logbook. Data used in the run: example. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
